Provenance of the non-local-means (NLM) code in this repository
=================================================================

This repository implements the non-local-means filter of

    Manjon, J. V., Coupe, P., Buades, A., Fonov, V., Collins, D. L., &
    Robles, M. (2010).  "Non-local MRI upsampling."
    Medical Image Analysis 14(6), 784-792.

Copyright (C) 2010 Jose V. Manjon and Pierrick Coupe.

The authors' own distribution of the method is Matlab plus a C MEX kernel,
`legacy/demo/NLMUpsample/linux-mac code/cMRegularizarNLM3D_V2.c`, which is
stated by its accompanying header to be GPL-licensed. Two things in this
repository descend from it:

`upsample/sr/nlm_core.c`
    A direct, MEX-free port of the same C kernel.

`upsample/sr_pytorch/regularize.py`
    A PyTorch reimplementation of the same computation, carrying none of the
    C kernel's code: it is written as whole-volume tensor operations rather
    than as the original's per-voxel loop. It also differs from the C
    kernel by convention, not only by expression: the C code visits each
    pair of voxels once and uses the *first* voxel's sigma/local mean for
    both directions of the symmetric update, while this gathers, visiting
    each ordered pair from both ends and using each centre's own -- the two
    are not meant to be reconciled. (Documented at greater length in the N3
    project this file's ``strength``/``floor_mode`` denoising extensions
    were themselves backported from, `torch_n3/blocks/denoise.py`.)

Both are nevertheless derivatives of a GPL-licensed work by descent, and are
recorded here as such. Anyone redistributing this repository should settle
this against the terms of any other license applied to the rest of the
codebase before doing so.
